  "known_discrepancies": [
    "decode gemv_bw ms_per_token / effective_BW_GBs (analysis.json, effective_bandwidth.md, bandwidth_investigation/verdict.md) divide total GEMV time by tokens_estimated = max(FA_tile//17, GDN_FWHT//48) = 82..83 instead of n_predict = 64 (server predicted_n, the ground-truth decode token count). This inflates reported decode bandwidth by ~1.28x. Corrected IQ3_XXS effective BW is ~271-274 GB/s (43-44% of nominal 624 GB/s, ~52% of the measured 525 GB/s VRAM ceiling), not 349.8-351.6 GB/s. Q3_K corrected is ~393 GB/s (63% nominal, ~75% of ceiling), not 503.6 GB/s (96%). Corrected per-quant values per arm are in corrected_decode_BW. Qualitative conclusions (not at hardware limit; Q3_K faster than IQ3_XXS due to zero dependent gather loads) still hold.",
    "IQ4_XS decode 'bandwidth' (~1.9-2.4 TB/s, >100% of nominal) is a cache artifact (IQ4_XS weights are small, 217 MB total, resident in L2/IC); not a real VRAM stream. Marked UNCERTAIN in effective_bandwidth.md.",
    "server prompt_n (161/1421/5341/10671) is smaller than summary.json prompt_tokens_payload (1792/17000/64000/128000); the analysis tables use prompt_n. Reason for the difference is not documented (UNCERTAIN)."
  ],
  "all_ok": false,
